long double is eight bytes EVERYWHERE, not only in its size.

PATCH 0001 CHANGED THE SIZE AND LEFT FIVE PLACES BEHIND. It sets LDOUBLE_SIZE
to 8 so the compiler is consistent with the eight-byte long double micro-c
gives it, and says why at length. arm64-gen.c went on deciding five separate
things as though the type were binary128:

  arm64_type_size    answered 4 -- a log2 size meaning SIXTEEN bytes -- so a
                     long double argument got a Q register and sixteen bytes
                     of stack for an eight-byte value
  load               moved it with `mov v.16b, v.16b` instead of `fmov d,d`
  gen_opf            sent every arithmetic operation and comparison to
                     __addtf3, __lttf2 and the rest
  gen_cvt_itof       sent int -> long double to __floatunsitf
  gen_cvt_ftoi       sent long double -> int to __fixunstfsi
  gen_cvt_ftof       sent double <-> long double to __extenddftf2/__trunctfdf2

Each reads or writes sixteen bytes of a type that occupies eight.

MEASURED, and every failure is silent rather than loud:

    long double y = x;          x = 5.008
    y                           5000000000000000
    (expect)                    4014083126e978d5

WHERE IT BIT. musl's printf reads every floating-point argument into a long
double member --

    case DBL: arg->f = va_arg(*ap, double); break;      vfprintf.c, pop_arg

-- so printf("%f", 5.008) formatted garbage and gave 0.000000, and __floatscan
returns long double on the way out of strtod, so strtod("5.008") did not
compare equal to its own literal. Both measured at rung 3 of the stage-4
ladder:

    literal 5.008      = 0.000000  (expect 5.008000)
    5.008 == strtod    = 0         (expect 1)
    snprintf %.6f      = 0.000000  (expect 5.008000)

while three lines below, the same value's bits were exact and the same value
arrived through varargs intact:

    5.008 raw bits     = 40140831 26e978d5
    through varargs    = 40140831 26e978d5

THAT PAIR IS WHAT NAMED IT, and it is why the probe was added: printf cannot
distinguish "the value never arrived" from "the formatter is broken", because
both print 0.000000. With the constant right and the argument passing right,
only the relationship between the two float types was left -- and that is the
one thing patch 0001 changed and did not finish changing.

FIXING ONE SITE AT A TIME WOULD HAVE SHIPPED FOUR BROKEN COMPILERS. Correcting
gen_cvt_ftof alone left long double PARAMETERS wrong, because conversion and
classification are separate decisions. Correcting those two broke the
SELF-COMPILATION FIXPOINT: tcc folds an integer constant into a float with

    vtop->c.ld = (uint32_t)vtop->c.i;                   tccgen.c:3303

so a tcc COMPILED BY mc-tcc ran that through __floatunsitf and every
`(double)1000` it folded came out zero -- while mc-tcc itself, compiled by
micro-c, got it right. gen2.o and gen3.o then disagreed by exactly those two
constants, at the same offset the float gap has always shown up at. The five
sites are one change and are made together.

WHAT THE CHANGE IS. With the two types identical in representation, double to
long double is a no-op, float to long double is the ordinary fcvt, arithmetic
is the ordinary double path, and the size is three rather than four. Every
guard is on LDOUBLE_SIZE == 8, so a tcc built normally -- where long double
really is binary128 -- keeps the helpers and the wide classification.

IT ALSO REMOVES A DEPENDENCY. Before this, `long double y = x;` in any program
mc-tcc compiled emitted a call to __extenddftf2 and would not link without
libtcc1.a. It now needs neither.

MEASURED, ON A CLEAN CHECKOUT OF main, EITHER SIDE:

    difftest amd64       101 pass, 0 fail, 3 known gaps      unchanged
    difftest aarch64     103 pass, 0 fail, 3 known gaps      unchanged
    stage 2 corpus       419 of 426                          unchanged
    macro encodings, 64-bit immediates, the zzb widening     unchanged
    tests2 through mc-tcc 96 of 105, 0 float-blocked         unchanged
    self-compilation     gen2.o == gen3.o == gen4.o          restored
    archive, dynamic output, hosted link                     unchanged

    long double conversions, all five directions             now correct
    (double)1000 folded by gen2                              now correct

